# .dockerignore generated by Forge at import time, beside the Dockerfile it
# belongs to, and yours to edit on the same terms.
#
# A denylist rather than an allowlist: this image builds the application from
# source, so the source has to reach the build context. What is excluded is
# what would be wrong to carry in.

# Version control and Forge's own control files.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.forge
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# A dependency tree installed on someone's laptop is the wrong tree for this
# image: the build stage installs from the repository's own lockfile.
node_modules
*.log

# LOCAL dotenv files only. A committed .env or .env.production is deliberately
# NOT excluded — a build that reads one would otherwise change behaviour
# silently between a developer's machine and this image — while the *.local
# convention is the one every framework here reserves for secrets, and those
# must never enter a published image.
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Build output. The image regenerates it, so a committed copy is dead weight
# in the context and busts the layer cache on every unrelated change.
.next
